# Profile "ai-node": the knowledge-genome-orchestrator's AI node, a guest.
#
# Copied from the laptop by scripts/host-config-copy.sh into
# ${MEDIA_ROOT}/host-configs/<alias>/, which the `work` set takes off-site.
# One path per line; a leading `?` marks a path that may be absent, `~/` the
# login user's home. docs/backup.md, "Other machines".
#
# Everything else comes back without a backup: the orchestrator's repository
# and its deploy/ai-node scripts rebuild the runtime, the genome checkouts are
# copies of the forge, the models are downloaded again.

# The one file no repository holds: the bots' tokens, the models, the paths
~/.config/knowledge-genome.env

# The automation key and its forced command
?~/.ssh/authorized_keys

# The wrappers as installed — what really runs, which may differ from the
# repository
?/usr/local/bin/n8n-pi-wrap
?/usr/local/bin/kg-idle-check

# The model server's own settings: address, models directory
?/etc/systemd/system/ollama.service.d
